# Boardsource lulu: its raw HID interface becomes /dev/lulu-bridge, and the
# logged-in user may open it, so the quickshell bridge
# (retro/services/qmk/qmk-bridge.py) can talk to the board.
#
# USB ids match host/boards/lulu.json.  QMK always puts raw HID on USB
# interface 1 (tmk_core/protocol/usb_descriptor.h); the board's other hidraw
# nodes (keyboard, mouse, console) are left alone.  ENV{ID_*} rather than
# ATTRS{} because the vendor/product ids and the interface number live on
# different parent devices, and ATTRS keys must all match the same one; the
# ENV values are imported by 60-persistent-hidraw.rules.  The "70-" keeps this
# file ahead of 73-seat-late.rules, which turns the uaccess tag into an ACL.
# Installed by setup.sh.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="4273", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="7685", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="01", TAG+="uaccess", SYMLINK+="lulu-bridge"
